    <string name="settings_about">About Us</string>
    <string name="about_body">Simplify Your Audio Experience With Volume Control Launcher. This All-In-One App Offers A Powerful Volume Booster For Loud Sound, A Safe Audio Limit Feature To Protect Your Speakers, And System Sound Controls For Ringtones, Alarms, And More. Enjoy An Intuitive Interface For Easy Control And Boost Your Device\'s Volume With One Swipe From Your Homescreen.</string>
    <string name="settings_faq">FAQ</string>
    <string name="faq_title">Frequently Asked Questions</string>
    <string name="faq_tag_home">Default home screen</string>
    <string name="faq_home_button">Default Home Screen</string>
    <string name="faq_one_ui">One UI Home</string>
    <string name="faq_q1">Why do my home screen icons and widgets appear disorganized after I start using this launcher?</string>
    <string name="faq_a1">Your system launcher and our launcher operate independently and do not share data. <b> Volume Control</b> uses its own layout rules, and our design team has created a new home screen layout, so the arrangement may differ from what you are used to. However, we do not modify your system\'s original launcher in any way. If you prefer your previous layout, you can switch back to it at any time.</string>
    <string name="faq_q2">How can I quickly restore my original layout?</string>
    <string name="faq_a2">Our launcher does not change the settings of your system\'s default launcher. To restore your original home screen layout, go to <b>Settings → Apps → Volume Control → Home screen</b>. Under Home app, select One UI Home. This will set your original launcher as the default again.</string>
    <string name="faq_q3">Why does this launcher display so many ads?</string>
    <string name="faq_a3"><b>Keeping the app free:</b> This launcher is completely free, with no paid upgrades or mandatory subscriptions. Ads are our primary source of revenue and help cover server costs, development, updates, and routine maintenance.\n\n<b>Supporting feature development:</b> Features such as home screen layouts, animations, themes, wallpapers, icon packs, battery optimization, and privacy protection require ongoing investment. Ad revenue helps fund development, testing, and customer support.\n\n<b>Following a common industry model:</b> Advertising is a widely used way to support free launcher apps. We make every effort to manage the frequency and placement of ads to minimize disruption.</string>
    <string name="faq_q4">Are the ads safe? Could they steal my personal information?</string>
    <string name="faq_a4">We only integrate SDKs from authorized advertising platforms and strictly follow our privacy policy. We do not collect your home screen layout, app list, files, or any other private data through ads. We never automatically download unknown apps or access your account or personal information. You can use our service with confidence.</string>
    <string name="faq_q5">Does setting this launcher as the default affect my phone\'s security?</string>
    <string name="faq_a5">No. Setting this app as your default home screen simply tells the system to use it first. It does not access your private information, manage other permissions on your phone, or interfere with normal device use or system security.</string>
    <string name="faq_q6">Why does my phone ask me to choose a launcher every time I press the Home button?</string>
    <string name="faq_a6">This happens because no default launcher has been set, so the system asks you which launcher to use each time. When the selection dialog appears, choose \"Always\" or set this app as the default launcher. The prompt will then stop appearing.</string>
    <string name="faq_q7">Is this app a virus?</string>
    <string name="faq_a7">No. Our app is neither a virus nor malware. You can download and install it from the official Google Play Store.\n\nWe take the security of your device very seriously and continuously improve the app\'s security and user experience. If you suspect your phone is infected, you can download third-party antivirus software to scan it.\n\nThank you for your understanding and support.</string>
    <string name="faq_q8">Why does the app require certain permissions?</string>
    <string name="faq_a8">Some permissions are needed to enable specific features in the app. We follow the principle of least privilege and request permissions only when they are required for the relevant features.\n\nYou can view and manage the app\'s permissions in your phone\'s app permission settings.\n\nIf you have questions about a specific permission, please contact us to learn what it is used for.</string>
    <string name="faq_q9">How do I uninstall the app?</string>
    <string name="faq_a9">Go to <b>Settings</b> → <b>Apps</b>, find the app, and tap Uninstall. If you cannot uninstall the app because it is set as your default home screen (launcher), go to <b>Settings</b> → <b>Apps</b> → <b>Choose default apps</b> → <b>Home app</b>, select your system\'s default launcher, and then uninstall the app.\n\nThank you for your understanding and support.</string>
